1
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:21,720
...Time to get going!

2
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:24,250
...He's fast!

3
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:27,250
...From the double touch feint... he's going through here!

4
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:32,590
Here I go!

5
00:00:32,890 --> 00:00:34,430
The spinning aerial charge!

6
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:38,760
...I slipped behind them.

7
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:40,720
...You're amazing, Bachira!

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:41,850
...I can do this.

9
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:43,890
...Our style of football.

10
00:00:43,890 --> 00:00:45,980
It works against them too!

11
00:00:51,610 --> 00:00:52,820
...What?

12
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:54,320
No way...?

13
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,500
What brought him here...?

14
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:10,610
What an incredible clearance from Oliver Aiku!!!

15
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:13,970
...In this attack.

16
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:20,080
I think his defending was based on seeing the source of the pass plus the positioning\Nof all the players in front of the penalty area from the back line...

17
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:22,900
...and grasping it in an instant.

18
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:26,440
...Then running without hesitation towards our most dangerous shooting point.

19
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:32,850
...That reflexive reaction I want to use in front of the goal,\Nhe's using it masterfully in his defense!

20
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:37,440
...His field of vision... his intelligence... his physique.

21
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:43,040
The entire level of his defending is completely different from any defender I've faced before!

22
00:01:44,210 --> 00:01:46,330
...So this is what a real defender is like.

23
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:49,680
This is the essence of Oliver Aiku!

24
00:01:50,570 --> 00:01:51,860
They're going to take a throw-in!

25
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:55,140
...We have to crush him, otherwise...

26
00:01:55,810 --> 00:01:57,810
...we'll never win this match!

27
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:42,700
...No matter how much the three of us exchange passes in the deep, as long as Aiku is watching us...

28
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:45,470
...breaking through is going to be tough.

29
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:47,740
...In that case, we'll resort to an alternative solution!

30
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:49,040
...Our second option.

31
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:51,540
...Break through them from the right wing, Otoya!

32
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:54,910
...Got it...! Infiltration time!

33
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,840
...I sense something coming.

34
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:01,960
...All your movements are within my sight!

35
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:07,600
What's your deal, tattooed Buddha...?

36
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:09,640
...The field represents the principle of Yin and Yang.

37
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:12,690
...It has two parts... the front and the back.

38
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:18,530
...Those who receive the ball in the front.

39
00:04:18,530 --> 00:04:22,650
...And those who lurk in the shadows of the back for a chance at a single fatal strike.

40
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:25,740
...He's still keeping up with my off-the-ball movements!

41
00:04:26,030 --> 00:04:28,280
Too bad for you, ninja.

42
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:30,240
...Because I'm good at the same style!

43
00:04:32,390 --> 00:04:34,370
...I sense you, I sense you!

44
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:36,330
...This guy...

45
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:41,300
...He's perfectly predicting where I want to sneak in from!

46
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:45,930
Try facing me with more agile steps, clumsy ninja?

47
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:47,390
...How annoying.

48
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:50,850
Otoya... can't get past him...?

49
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,230
...I can't pass to him like this.

50
00:04:53,490 --> 00:04:55,230
Switch the play, Isagi!

51
00:04:55,350 --> 00:04:56,350
Right!

52
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:58,110
On to our next option then!

53
00:04:58,470 --> 00:04:59,950
...Go, left wing!

54
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:01,870
...Crush them in the one-on-ones!

55
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,280
Yukimiya!

56
00:05:03,870 --> 00:05:05,490
My turn at last!

57
00:05:06,950 --> 00:05:09,490
Your glasses are truly cool!

58
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:12,870
Thanks for the compliment, shorty.

59
00:05:18,210 --> 00:05:19,750
Bo-bo!

60
00:05:20,610 --> 00:05:21,900
This way?

61
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,710
You're faster than what's written in your data!

62
00:05:23,710 --> 00:05:26,050
This kid... Shouldn't I have gotten past him...?

63
00:05:27,420 --> 00:05:29,180
...So he's a fast defender.

64
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:31,560
This way?

65
00:05:32,610 --> 00:05:35,770
...I'm not the carnivorous type that relies on physical strength.

66
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:38,770
I'm a herbivorous defender who won't lose in a speed contest!

67
00:05:38,770 --> 00:05:42,250
You're a little aggressive for a herbivore.

68
00:05:42,730 --> 00:05:45,670
...Seriously...?! Even Yukimiya, the king of one-on-ones?

69
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:47,100
Here...?

70
00:05:47,670 --> 00:05:49,410
He can't get past him...?

71
00:05:49,410 --> 00:05:50,830
...He's lightning fast!

72
00:05:50,830 --> 00:05:52,530
Who is that full-back...?

73
00:05:52,530 --> 00:05:53,540
Loose ball!

74
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:54,950
Got it!

75
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:58,170
...It's really tough to break into them.

76
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,520
...I'll receive it and turn, then...

77
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,130
As if I'd let you!

78
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:06,690
I won't let you run free, super-receiver!

79
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:11,800
...His pressing is so fast and intense!

80
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:14,170
...I can't turn towards the goal to continue the attack!

81
00:06:14,910 --> 00:06:17,830
...His pressing stifled Nagi's creativity in trapping!

82
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:21,280
This guy... he's a defender specialized in violent pressing!

83
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,310
Call me Doberman!

84
00:06:24,310 --> 00:06:26,190
Are you a guard dog or something...?

85
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:27,780
...Yes.

86
00:06:27,780 --> 00:06:29,530
And here comes my owner!

87
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:35,240
Good boy, Niou.

88
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:39,070
And now Aiku cuts it off?

89
00:06:39,070 --> 00:06:41,160
...What an incredible defensive cohesion!

90
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:45,460
...So this is the Iron Quartet defense of Japan U-20!

91
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:49,050
You look paralyzed, Blue Lock players?

92
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:55,600
...They got us...! One pass between the lines is enough for them to counter!

93
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,060
...And the one who's going to receive it is...

94
00:06:58,360 --> 00:06:59,850
Itoshi Sae!

95
00:07:01,730 --> 00:07:04,470
Now... show us what you've got, little genius.

96
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:07,110
...It's your time to shine!

97
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:11,870
And receiving the ball... Itoshi Sae!

98
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:14,370
What will he show us, I wonder?

99
00:07:14,370 --> 00:07:15,580
This is what I've been waiting for!

100
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:17,410
Break through them all!

101
00:07:18,830 --> 00:07:20,080
Someone stop him, quick!

102
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,620
Hold on!

103
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:21,620
What are you doing, you lunatics?!

104
00:07:22,110 --> 00:07:23,460
As if I'd let you pass!

105
00:07:24,130 --> 00:07:26,710
We have defensive measures for counter-attacks!

106
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:32,720
When Bachira goes forward to attack, I pull back to cover him, and vice versa!

107
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:35,140
....I'll use my speed to sto-

108
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:37,930
He already passed...?

109
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,910
How fast he decided!

110
00:07:39,910 --> 00:07:46,990
He hit a medium-speed long pass over 50 meters...?

111
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:50,840
In...credible!

112
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:56,410
I'll be... your opponent... mannequin boy!

113
00:07:56,410 --> 00:07:57,410
...No.

114
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,090
Kitsune!

115
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,790
Great!

116
00:08:01,050 --> 00:08:03,210
Let's move forward quickly and without wasting time!

117
00:08:04,050 --> 00:08:05,580
As we expected.

118
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:07,540
Come at me, dwarf!

119
00:08:07,540 --> 00:08:08,850
As you expected?

120
00:08:08,850 --> 00:08:11,170
It's all the same to us!

121
00:08:13,090 --> 00:08:14,230
...Wow!

122
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:18,030
Itoshi Sae is free in front of the goal and has space to shoot!

123
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:22,780
An attacking pattern that starts with Itoshi Sae and ends with him!

124
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:27,400
That was their aim from the counter!

125
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,360
Niko!

126
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:29,310
I've got this!

127
00:08:30,430 --> 00:08:33,700
...Don't let him shoot! Delay him even for a second... just until...

128
00:08:33,970 --> 00:08:35,640
Chigiri-kun can get back!

129
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,610
Nice, Niko!

130
00:08:37,610 --> 00:08:40,040
We've surrounded him...! We stopped Itoshi Sae!

131
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,500
...A light chip pass.

132
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:49,750
Through that tiny gap between us...?

133
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:52,460
Just how far does his vision reach?!

134
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:53,650
Hell yeah!

135
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:55,340
Gagamaru!

136
00:08:55,390 --> 00:08:56,720
Whoa! He's going to shoot!

137
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:01,650
Jump, my nerve cells!

138
00:09:01,650 --> 00:09:03,310
And trigger my super reflexes!

139
00:09:04,090 --> 00:09:06,490
Gagamaru Punch!

140
00:09:06,490 --> 00:09:07,250
...What?

141
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:08,540
Great job, Gagamaru!

142
00:09:09,770 --> 00:09:12,480
The ball is still in play! And Itoshi Sae is going for it!

143
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:14,240
He's running in advance!

144
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:16,360
He's coming again! Watch out for the cross!

145
00:09:18,950 --> 00:09:21,160
...He has no angle to pass from!

146
00:09:21,550 --> 00:09:22,910
It'll be fine!

147
00:09:43,630 --> 00:09:45,340
...Incredible!

148
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:50,270
A spinning vertical shot from that position...?

149
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:56,170
What's more... what's with the accuracy of his passing ever since he received the ball...?

150
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:59,950
...Holy crap.

151
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:06,160
Japan U-20 National Team opens the scoring through Itoshi Sae's feet!!!

152
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:08,750
The cheers of the crowd in the stadium have erupted!!!

153
00:10:10,170 --> 00:10:15,270
Sae! Sae! Sae! Sae! Sae!

154
00:10:15,270 --> 00:10:16,830
...This reaction...

155
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:19,090
...It's exactly like playing an away game.

156
00:10:19,090 --> 00:10:20,390
...Damn it!

157
00:10:22,470 --> 00:10:24,530
...I get it now.

158
00:10:25,870 --> 00:10:29,980
...The sole star of this match is... Itoshi Sae.

159
00:10:37,060 --> 00:10:39,160
...And in their eyes, we are...

160
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:43,600
...nothing but villains fighting against Itoshi Sae!

161
00:10:48,110 --> 00:10:52,920
...And not one of them... cares about us... in the slightest.

162
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:56,420
Itoshi Sae!! Itoshi Sae!

163
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:57,880
...Don't get swallowed up by the crowd's noise, Isagi.

164
00:10:58,110 --> 00:11:05,970
Itoshi Sae!! Itoshi Sae!! Itoshi Sae!! Itoshi Sae!

165
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:03,040
...Just watch me.

166
00:11:04,850 --> 00:11:09,700
Within these ninety minutes... I'll turn those cheers\Nof joy and admiration... into screams of pain, suffering, and regret!!!

167
00:11:11,090 --> 00:11:11,980
...Rin!

168
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:18,090
...Itoshi Sae is truly a genius!

169
00:11:18,090 --> 00:11:20,340
What a debut for his first appearance!

170
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:22,530
That's the extent of Itoshi Sae's prowess!

171
00:11:22,530 --> 00:11:22,960
You're right!

172
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:27,410
We might be witnessing the birth of a hero today!

173
00:11:27,410 --> 00:11:28,200
We just might!

174
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:30,170
That was an incredible shot!

175
00:11:30,170 --> 00:11:32,180
What a fantastic goal, Sae-kun!

176
00:11:32,180 --> 00:11:33,750
Don't you dare touch me, you lowlife!

177
00:11:35,430 --> 00:11:36,380
...Three.

178
00:11:37,850 --> 00:11:40,810
...That's the number of chances I could have shot.

179
00:11:41,490 --> 00:11:47,350
But I held back and wasted my precious time and effort passing to you all.

180
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:52,320
...But because that piece of trash missed a goal even a monkey could score,

181
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:54,100
I got pissed off and scored myself.

182
00:11:54,980 --> 00:11:57,530
Monkey...?! Trash...?!

183
00:11:58,070 --> 00:12:02,530
Calm down! Their goalkeeper just made a brilliant save, that's all!

184
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:06,950
What's the point of a forward if he can't score?

185
00:12:07,340 --> 00:12:10,840
...If your goal average is lower than mine, a midfielder,

186
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:13,420
...you're not a forward in my dictionary.

187
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:15,660
That's way too harsh, little genius.

188
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:19,460
If you say that, then how many forwards are there in Japan?

189
00:12:19,770 --> 00:12:22,380
...We're playing this match to discover that.

190
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:26,050
Don't you dare do that again, you wretch lower than a monkey.

191
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:32,520
Calm down! The match just started, Sendou!

192
00:12:33,470 --> 00:12:35,230
Don't waste other chances!

193
00:12:35,550 --> 00:12:37,160
...I know that, Aiku.

194
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:40,900
Japan U-20... is my team!

195
00:12:44,910 --> 00:12:48,140
Damn...! Even though I saved the first one.

196
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:51,220
It was a glam save! Mr. Super Reflexes!

197
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:53,870
I saw it!

198
00:12:53,870 --> 00:12:57,330
Even so... can he score from that position...?

199
00:12:57,720 --> 00:13:00,290
...A solid defense followed by a fast counter-attack.

200
00:13:00,650 --> 00:13:05,280
...Thanks to Itoshi Sae, their team has become many times stronger.

201
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:06,340
...Right.

202
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:11,310
...First... they tightened their defense using four defenders.

203
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:16,020
...Then they stole the ball from us while we were looking for a way to break through.

204
00:13:16,250 --> 00:13:19,960
...Then they launched a fast counter-attack through Itoshi Sae.

205
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:25,080
...This is the playing style of the Japan U-20 National Team.

206
00:13:26,910 --> 00:13:28,350
How can we destroy it...?

207
00:13:30,150 --> 00:13:35,040
...The plans we trained on at camp aren't working at all!

208
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:38,160
Are we going to be alright, Ego-san...?

209
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:40,630
Well, this is somewhat expected.

210
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:43,050
Where does this nonchalance come from...?

211
00:13:43,050 --> 00:13:46,130
Training is just training, Anri-chan.

212
00:13:47,130 --> 00:13:49,660
...The necessity of training is limited only to...

213
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:52,680
...displaying your skills in an environment free of pressure.

214
00:13:53,190 --> 00:13:57,440
...And it's the same all over the world... a person can put on a really great performance in training.

215
00:13:58,310 --> 00:14:00,620
But they don't deliver the same performance on the real stage.

216
00:14:02,610 --> 00:14:04,590
...I think I experienced that before.

217
00:14:04,590 --> 00:14:07,150
...When I failed while playing the piano.

218
00:14:07,150 --> 00:14:08,540
Exactly, exactly.

219
00:14:09,310 --> 00:14:14,330
The fundamental difference between training and real match application... is the presence of pressure.

220
00:14:15,610 --> 00:14:21,750
...The field... the opponent... your physical condition...

221
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:27,770
...your psychological changes... your muscle tension... the disruption of your train of thought...

222
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:33,130
The real field is full of factors that can drag you into a downward spiral.

223
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:36,800
...And it's almost impossible for things to go exactly as you trained.

224
00:14:37,660 --> 00:14:41,270
...And there's only one way to overcome this kind of pressure.

225
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:43,480
Improvisation.

226
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:47,090
Aren't you going to give them any instructions?

227
00:14:47,090 --> 00:14:48,790
...But if you just keep watching, then...

228
00:14:48,790 --> 00:14:50,710
Just shut up and trust them.

229
00:14:50,710 --> 00:14:52,990
...Our egoist players...

230
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,700
...are strong on the real stage!

231
00:15:00,130 --> 00:15:03,080
...I still can't see the missing piece to break through their defense.

232
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:06,580
...For me... they're an unknown, strong opponent.

233
00:15:07,230 --> 00:15:08,050
...But!

234
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:11,540
...Just watch me.

235
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:14,430
...I know exactly what I need to do.

236
00:15:14,790 --> 00:15:16,610
...I'll ignore unnecessary thoughts.

237
00:15:17,070 --> 00:15:19,520
...And mobilize everything I'm capable of doing.

238
00:15:20,740 --> 00:15:23,460
...In synergy with Rin!

239
00:15:26,350 --> 00:15:30,280
...Exchanging passes in midfield is futile, you know... ha.

240
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:34,660
...You seem lost, not knowing who to pass to... ha.

241
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:36,910
...Keep barking, dark circles boy.

242
00:15:40,450 --> 00:15:42,500
A shorter pass...?

243
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:45,460
Does he want to change our attacking pattern...?

244
00:15:46,220 --> 00:15:48,380
So you won't be using your triangle anymore.

245
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:50,210
...Ignore the others.

246
00:15:50,580 --> 00:15:52,430
...And focus only on the frenzy.

247
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,140
Within Rin's field of vision!

248
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:55,850
Their passing tempo increased?

249
00:15:58,050 --> 00:16:00,060
...I can't read their movements.

250
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:04,070
...Number 11 keeps running around Number 10.

251
00:16:04,070 --> 00:16:07,770
...Which expands Number 10's options and makes it harder for me to keep up with him!

252
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:09,940
Disaster!

253
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:11,490
Now a backheel pass?!

254
00:16:12,250 --> 00:16:13,910
They trapped us!

255
00:16:16,530 --> 00:16:19,040
Your synergy makes me so jealous!

256
00:16:19,390 --> 00:16:24,330
And now your plan is to run freely toward the goal, right?

257
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:27,840
...There are only two defenders behind Nagi!

258
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:31,370
It's become three against two...! We have the numerical advantage!

259
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:33,190
It's a guaranteed scoring opportunity!

260
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:37,510
...From here... I'll follow my egoism!

261
00:16:37,510 --> 00:16:39,890
They're separating now?!

262
00:16:39,890 --> 00:16:41,930
I don't understand those two!

263
00:16:41,930 --> 00:16:43,940
Let's stop them together, Aiku!

264
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:48,130
What wonderful movements, little thief.

265
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:50,530
Now! Pass it to me!

266
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:53,280
No... over there!

267
00:16:54,030 --> 00:16:55,070
This one's for you, avenger!

268
00:16:59,550 --> 00:17:00,690
They broke through!

269
00:17:00,690 --> 00:17:03,640
Nice improvisation, Itoshi Rin.

270
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:07,460
Your awakening is what will lead us to victory!

271
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:13,470
He's coming! He's going to shoot now!

272
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:17,050
He went even deeper inside?

273
00:17:17,050 --> 00:17:18,760
He took a route with no shooting angle...?

274
00:17:19,550 --> 00:17:20,930
And he's going to shoot with his left too...?

275
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:25,640
Is he trying to replicate Itoshi Sae's goal himself...?

276
00:17:32,150 --> 00:17:34,110
Good save! Watch out for the loose ball!

277
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:38,870
...Here it comes.

278
00:17:39,830 --> 00:17:40,920
I won't let you pass!

279
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:42,570
You again?

280
00:17:42,570 --> 00:17:45,330
This is the offensive situation we trained for!

281
00:17:45,870 --> 00:17:49,250
...I'll enter the field of vision of the defender marking Yukimiya.

282
00:17:49,250 --> 00:17:54,710
...To create the illusion that I'm a potential passing option, just to make him hesitate for a second!

283
00:17:54,710 --> 00:17:56,840
Ah...! Damn it! From which direction...?

284
00:17:58,360 --> 00:18:00,010
...I was late to react!

285
00:18:00,350 --> 00:18:03,220
You were brilliant, Isagi-kun! I owe you one.

286
00:18:06,730 --> 00:18:07,950
Beautiful shot.

287
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:09,850
Even that wasn't enough to score?

288
00:18:09,850 --> 00:18:11,770
Clear it, Darai!

289
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:12,880
I know!

290
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,110
Hey!

291
00:18:14,110 --> 00:18:17,200
You took your eyes off me, stupid!

292
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:20,250
Otoya quickly responded to the loose ball in front of the goal!

293
00:18:20,250 --> 00:18:21,700
This is just as we trained!

294
00:18:22,380 --> 00:18:26,380
Rin's egoistic improvisation is what got us here!

295
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:30,770
...And now that we've disrupted their formation... we can take advantage!

296
00:18:31,140 --> 00:18:32,630
From our training!

297
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:38,720
Seriously?! Ah, you old man!

298
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:40,990
They're so tough...! But it's not over yet.

299
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:41,720
Nagi!

300
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:42,660
Got it!

301
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:45,560
...A huge chance!

302
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:46,920
We won't let you shoot!

303
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:47,890
Yeah!

304
00:18:48,170 --> 00:18:49,980
...I'll fake a shot, then...

305
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:53,650
...stop the ball.

306
00:18:55,420 --> 00:18:56,610
He flicked the ball with his left foot...?

307
00:19:00,050 --> 00:19:02,530
Then followed up with a spinning jump...?

308
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:08,200
Nice to meet you, people of Japan.

309
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:10,120
...My name is...

310
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:13,960
Nagi Seishiro!!!

311
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:31,030
...Wow.

312
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:35,180
Did my introduction not reach them...?

313
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:43,990
Yessss!!!!

314
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,450
Seriously...?

315
00:19:57,450 --> 00:19:58,920
...Not bad.

316
00:20:00,070 --> 00:20:04,640
...I see... they care about nothing but scoring goals.

317
00:20:05,490 --> 00:20:08,510
...So this is Blue Lock.

318
00:20:10,930 --> 00:20:14,320
...If this project really succeeds... it's going to be devastating!

319
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:54,020
Blue Lock: Additional Time!

320
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:06,380
Hey! Long time no see! How are you?

321
00:22:08,710 --> 00:22:11,450
Hey there, partner! Let's play together again!

322
00:22:15,310 --> 00:22:18,390
You're not my teammate anymore!

323
00:22:18,690 --> 00:22:21,200
Damn...! What am I supposed to do?

324
00:22:21,690 --> 00:22:23,400
What are you doing, Reo...?

325
00:22:24,150 --> 00:22:25,010
Chigiri!

326
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:28,910
Did copying other people's movements so much give you dissociative identity disorder?

327
00:22:28,910 --> 00:22:30,410
No, no, no!

328
00:22:30,660 --> 00:22:32,960
...This... how do I explain it...

329
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:38,330
...I don't know what or how to talk to Nagi ever since we got back together, so I was practicing.

330
00:22:38,590 --> 00:22:41,640
Oh, I see! So you haven't talked to him yet?

331
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:45,210
...Yeah... not yet.

332
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:49,430
...I've become a chameleon who forgot its true color!

333
00:22:50,420 --> 00:22:53,150
You dog! At least show some interest!

334
00:22:53,150 --> 00:22:57,060
...I'm not worried since it's you, but...

335
00:22:57,320 --> 00:23:01,320
If you have something you want to tell him, say it while you still have the chance.

336
00:23:01,320 --> 00:23:04,730
...In this place, you never know if you'll see that person again or not.

337
00:23:05,570 --> 00:23:06,710
...Good evening.

338
00:23:07,620 --> 00:23:09,150
...O-Okay.

339
00:23:09,970 --> 00:23:11,400
...I see.

340
00:23:12,480 --> 00:23:13,930
...He's right.

341
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:17,570
...What I really want to say is...

342
00:23:18,630 --> 00:23:23,420
Nagi... how do you feel about me right now...?

343
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:25,960
...To you, am I...

344
00:23:26,190 --> 00:23:27,460
A partner?

345
00:23:27,460 --> 00:23:28,880
Or a rival?

346
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:30,380
A comrade?

347
00:23:30,620 --> 00:23:31,880
Or a foe?

348
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:33,760
Or just someone from the past...?

349
00:23:34,970 --> 00:23:38,840
Don't mess with me!! You dare make me just a part of the past?

350
00:23:38,840 --> 00:23:41,580
Got you! I'll make you pay, you annoying monster!

351
00:23:42,050 --> 00:23:45,060
...You're the biggest annoyance here.